This product includes design and implementation patterns adapted from the
Android Open Source Project (AOSP) Launcher3, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0:

    https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/apps/Launcher3/
    Copyright (C) The Android Open Source Project

Launcher3 is a View-system application; the patterns below were re-implemented
from scratch in Jetpack Compose for this project (the model was adapted, not
the code copied verbatim):

  - the drag layer / drag controller model (cross-surface icon drag between
    the workspace, dock and app drawer);
  - live drop feedback and drop targets;
  - folders (drop icon-on-icon), notification dots, and pinned deep shortcuts;
  - the widget edit frame (resize / move / remove / reconfigure), adapted from
    AppWidgetResizeFrame, DeleteDropTarget and isReconfigurable;
  - widget size options for hosted widgets (so collection widgets populate),
    adapted from WidgetSizes.getWidgetSizeOptions; and the scrollable-content
    check, adapted from LauncherAppWidgetHostView.checkScrollableRecursively.

This project does not include source code from Lawnchair; only high-level
concepts were studied from it (current Lawnchair is Apache-2.0). The
implementations here are original.

Weather data in the clock widget is provided by Open-Meteo
(https://open-meteo.com/), licensed under CC BY 4.0.

The imported upstream source included a reference to BigDataCloud's free
client-side reverse-geocoding API (https://www.bigdatacloud.com/). Nomina no
longer calls this API; this attribution is retained to preserve the upstream notice.
